# Log Analysis with SIEM – TryHackMe

## Project Overview

This repository documents my completion of the **Log Analysis with SIEM** room on TryHackMe. The project focuses on understanding how 
Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) solutions collect, normalize, correlate, and analyze security logs to detect malicious 
activities and support incident investigations.

Through hands-on exercises, I gained practical experience using Splunk to investigate security events, identify suspicious behavior, and
understand the role of SIEM platforms within Security Operations Centers (SOC).


## Learning Objectives

* Understand the purpose and value of SIEM solutions.
* Analyze security logs from multiple data sources.
* Use Splunk queries to detect malicious activities.
* Learn the fundamentals of event correlation.
* Understand log normalization processes.
* Investigate security incidents using SIEM technologies.
* Develop foundational SOC analyst skills.


